# Files colours for a partly staged file and a partly staged directory. Kept as
# its own flow: lazygit's rule for a file staged and modified again (MM) is not
# in the other flows' screenshots, and a directory with one of two files staged
# is the yellow case. Names are green only for fully staged files.
repo .
focus "colours of the Files rows by staging state: an MM file (staged, then modified again) and a directory with only one of its two files staged; letters, names and the arrow of each row, selected and not"
not "how the panels are sized, launch screen, mouse and scrolling (ui-mouse); commit workflows (stage-commit, feature-workflow); Space on a directory (stage-directory)"

sh "git reset -q --hard && git clean -fdq && git checkout -q main"
sh "printf '\nfirst edit\n' >> README.md; mkdir -p Zdir; printf 'x\n' > Zdir/one.txt; printf 'y\n' > Zdir/two.txt"
note "README.md is modified and Zdir/ holds two untracked files. Nothing is staged."

step 01_start
step 02_focus_files 2
step 03_on_readme j
note "Stage README.md: a fully staged file, letter and name."
step 04_stage_readme Space

sh "printf 'second edit\n' >> README.md"
note "An editor changed README.md again behind the programs' back: it is now staged and modified (MM). Look at the letters and the name."
step 05_readme_mm 2

note "Move to Zdir/one.txt and stage it: the directory now has one staged and one untracked file."
step 06_on_one j j
step 07_stage_one Space
note "Select the last file so the root, the directory, README.md (MM) and one.txt are all drawn unselected."
step 08_move_away j
